Well, what could be stupider than trying to perform a Stupid Ascension
Trick? Trying to do a full set of them. The idea of ascending using
only
the weapons and armor specific to a race was mentioned by Robin
Johnson in December 2004. I finally got around to including all of the
non-human possibilities in version 0.6 of the list of Stupid Ascension
Tricks. (http://thinksystem.net/nethack)

I started thinking about trying one of these. Dwarf sounded the
easiest.
Then it occurred to me: if I was going to do one of them, why not do
them all? ('Cause it is hard. And stupid.) It took a number of months
and quite a few games, but, I did it. The four ascension posts will
follow in additional postings.

This was a learning experience. I learned to have much more respect for
mumakil and zruties than I used to. They hit hard for the levels at
which they appear. Even when I managed to have a bit of armor class
when I first encountered them, they would kill me or come close. I
learned to be pretty good at the protection racket (trying a naked
Gnome gave plenty of pratice. I learned to be patient and wait for
my pets if I was still low level. I learned to use Elbereth. A lot.

I'm not sure this was fun, but it was interesting.

